      r =  420 kpc:  x-curve resid -0.282 (std 0.152)    c_dust +0.378 (std 0.108)
      r =  600 kpc:  x-curve resid -0.419 (std 0.163)    c_dust +0.205 (std 0.141)
  Spearman(mean x-curve resid, r/R500) = -1.000 (p = 0.000);  Spearman(mean c_dust, r/R500) = -1.000 (p = 0.000)
  (the absolute-kpc envelope above conflates the R500 spreading; the r/R500 form is fitted per cluster below)

  (b) the mass-ordering: cluster-mean residuals vs M500
  Spearman(cluster-mean x-curve resid, M500) = +0.385 (p = 0.217)
  Spearman(cluster-mean c_dust, M500)        = -0.273 (p = 0.391)

  (c) THE 2D FORM: log10 c_dust(M500, r/R500) = const + q log10 M500   - p log10(r/R500).  (c_dust = the theory-curve residual level.)
  fit (96 bins, 3 params): const = -0.145, q = d log10 c_dust/d log10 M500 = -0.414, p = -d log10 c_dust/d log10(r/R500) = +0.990;  residual rms = 0.119 dex
  -> the 2D form: c_dust = 0.72 (M500/8e14)^-0.414 (r/R500)^-0.990

