STEP 3 -- THE CLOSED-FORM CANDIDATE: ONE per-cluster normalization + ONE universal shape p (the <0.15-dex collapse question)
====================================================================================================
  model:  R(x, r) = [2x/(x-1)] * a_c * (r/R500)^-p          (free-dust normalization a_c per cluster, ONE profile shape p pooled)
  =>  log10 R = log10[2x/(x-1)] + log10 a_c - p log10(r/R500)
  grid over p in [-4, 4]: best UNIVERSAL shape p* = +0.990
  achieved collapse (one shape p*, one amplitude per cluster): rms = 0.097 dex
  [PASS] P0 [the closed-form candidate gate: with ONE per-cluster normalization and ONE universal shape p the residual curve's scatter collapses below 0.15 dex] achieved rms about the closed form 2x/(x-1) * a_c * (r/R500)^-p, p fitted pooled
         measured: rms = 0.097 dex (p* = +0.99; 13 parameters on 96 bins; gate < 0.15)
         reading : the honest number: the achieved collapse with ONE shape p and free per-cluster amplitude
  BASELINE p = 0 (per-cluster amplitude only, no radial shape): rms = 0.361 dex -- the radial shape p* buys 0.264 dex of collapse
  the per-bin 16-84 half-width at p*: 0.097 dex
  per-cluster rms at the best-fit (one shape p*): max = 0.143 dex (RXC1825); 12/12 clusters with per-cluster rms < 0.15 dex
  per-cluster free-dust amplitudes log10 a_c (the 2D statement's mass side):
    A1644      log10 a_c = -0.011
    A1795      log10 a_c = -0.131
