    ZW1215     log10 a_c = -0.064
  Spearman(log10 a_c, M500) = -0.587 (p = 0.045) -- the per-cluster amplitude IS mass-ordered
  THE 3-PARAMETER CLOSED FORM  log10 c_dust = const + q log10 M500 + p log10(r/R500):  q = -0.414, p = +0.990, achieved rms = 0.119 dex  (no per-cluster freedom at all)

  THE COLLAPSE LADDER (rms of log10 R about each closed form):
    G105 pooled x-space curve (0 shots)                         0.313 dex
    theory 2x/(x-1) alone (0 params)                            0.368 dex
    2x/(x-1) * a_c, p = 0 (12 amps)                             0.361 dex
    2x/(x-1) * a_c * (r/R500)^-p, p pooled (12 amps + 1 p)      0.097 dex
    2x/(x-1) * c0*M500^q * (r/R500)^-p (3 params)               0.119 dex

====================================================================================================
V -- THE VERDICTS
====================================================================================================
  [PASS] V1 [the ordering property] the cluster property that orders the pooled residual (largest |rho|, with its p)
         measured: THE ORDERING.  (i) RADIAL first: the pooled x-curve residual is monotone in r/R500 -- Spearman -1.000 (p ~ 0.000) over the 8 radii, ++0.44 dex at 50 kpc falling to -0.42 dex at 600 kpc: the dominant pattern of the 0.313-dex scatter is the RADIAL ENVELOPE (the free-dust profile shape the x-curve does not absorb).  (ii) MASS side: among the cluster properties the residual LEVELS order by f_gas(420) (rho = +0.497, p = 0.101) > M500 (rho = +0.385, p = 0.217) > r_M/R500 (rho = +0.336, p = 0.286) > kTvir (rho = +0.294, p = 0.354) > the a0-crossing radius (rho = +0.224, p = 0.533, n = 10; A1644/A2255 none).  On the free-dust basis (log10 c_dust) the SAME ordering holds with reversed signs: f_gas(420) rho = -0.413 (p = 0.183); no property is significant at p < 0.05 at the cluster-mean level (n = 12 power), the per-bin cross-check marks f_gas(420) at p = 0.021 (nominal).
  [PASS] V2 [the achieved collapse with ONE shape p, per-cluster amplitude free] rms about the closed form
         measured: p* = +0.990, rms = 0.097 dex; < 0.15 -> True
         reading : the closed-form candidate with the phantom (2x/(x-1)) + the dust-normalization shape c_dust(M500)(r/R500)^-p
  [PASS] V3 [the honest statement] is the free-dust normalization ONE profile shape with per-cluster amplitude?
         measured: HONEST: the free-dust normalization IS ONE profile shape (r/R500)^-0.99 with a per-cluster amplitude: the closed form closes the curve to 0.097 dex.  The collapse ladder: pooled x-curve 0.313 -> theory-only 0.368 -> +12 amps 0.361 -> + shape p 0.097 -> full 3-param closed form 0.119 dex.  Thorn freedom remaining: the amplitude freedom is the remaining thorn -- but even with NO per-cluster freedom the literal form c0*M500^q*(r/R500)^-p closes at 0.119 dex (q = -0.41 from the fit, one p = +0.99 for all 12), and the per-cluster slopes spread only 0.27 around their median -0.92 (the 13-parameter fit relaxes this to 0.097 dex, 12/12 clusters inside 0.15); what remains OPEN is the residual floor of the amplitude itself (what sets q, and the A1644/A2255 pair with no a0-crossing sits outside the ordering).

